---
description: PayProof engineering rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- Money is computed only in `payproof/policy.py` with `Decimal` (never float). Round half-up once, at the end.
- The model (`payproof/llm.py`) may only phrase text. It never sets status, amounts, or actions.
- Every material claim must cite record ids that exist in the case; `final_validator` enforces this.
- Actions go through `payproof/actions.py` state machine; authorization is checked server-side.
- Fixtures are synthetic. Regenerate with `python3 scripts/build_fixtures.py`; ground truth in `bench/ground_truth.json` is hand-written — never generate it from engine output.
- Before committing: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` and `python3 -m payproof.bench`.
